    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0712" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">880.00/7–1547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-15T13:00:00+01:00">July 15, 1947—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2799. Further to Deptel 2556, July 11, and my 2781, July 12,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d477-f1"/> I have received informal indication from very high FonOff
                    source that a recommendation may shortly be made to Bidault that the French take
                    the initiative in asking us for our views and our help in solving problems in
                    North Africa and Indochina. I can not at present forecast how Bidault will react
                    to the suggestion, but tactically it would be so much better if the initiative
                    were to come from the French that I feel strongly we should hold off for the
                    moment. I should know the answer within a week or ten days.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d477-f1" n="1" xml:id="d477-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed; it advised waiting until the end of the Conference of
                    European Economic Cooperation, then in session, as Foreign Minister Bidault was
                    engrossed in it (880.00/7–1247).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
